            "title": "Copper Nears Record as US-China Optimism Adds to Supply Woes",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "Signs the world\u2019s top two economies are set to reach an accord this week improve the outlook for consumption of the industrial metal at a time of heightened concerns over production setbacks from South America to Indonesia.  Prices on the London Metal Exchange rose as much as 1.2% to $11,094 a ton, roughly $10 shy of a record reached in May 2024, before paring some of the gains.  Copper has rallied by a quarter this year \u2014 recovering from a deep selloff triggered by President Donald Trump\u2019s trade war escalation \u2014 as investors focus on a tenuous balance for supplies of the metal that\u2019s key to global electrification efforts.",
